.TH heliosctl-streams-set-destination 1 0.5.0 "heliosctl 0.5.0" "Helios Manual"
.SH NAME
heliosctl\-streams\-set\-destination \- Set where a stream goes: an srt:// or srtla:// URL
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBheliosctl streams set\-destination\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-secrets\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-client\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-url\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDEVICE\fR> <\fISTREAM\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set where a stream goes: an srt:// or srtla:// URL.
.PP
A URL with an SRT passphrase must come from a file or stdin (\-\-url\-file \-), never the command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Check the input and print the request without sending it
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON document on stdout, and errors as JSON on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-secrets\fR
Show secrets in full: destinations\*(Aq and Wi\-Fi networks\*(Aq passphrases (else `***`)
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the stream is live (desired live) or stopped, and the change applied
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL (…/dev)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR [default: 60]
How long \-\-wait waits, in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-client\-token\fR \fI<CLIENT_TOKEN>\fR
Makes the change safe to retry (default: a new random one)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
The AWS profile: one that assumes helios\-operator [default: helios\-operator]
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
The AWS region [default: the profile\*(Aqs]
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
The URL, if it has no passphrase
.TP
\fB\-\-url\-file\fR \fI<URL_FILE>\fR
A file holding the URL, or \- for stdin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIDEVICE\fR>
A device ID (d\-…) or thing name (t\-…)
.TP
<\fISTREAM\fR>
The stream\*(Aqs name
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
